        "original_id": "2c899aff-a194-5cb3-b1e6-6ae24f8e3c0b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Akshay Kumar, Nagarjuna, Pooja Bhatt, Sonali Bendre, Anu Malik, Aadesh Shrivastava, John Abraham, Rimi Sen, Neha Dhupia, Paresh Rawal, Rajpal Yadav, Priyadarshan\n- Films: Angaaray, Garam Masala, Lahu Ke Do Rang, Insaaf, Daava, Tarazu, Barood, Zulmi\n- Topics: filmography, box office performance, death\n\nFacts:\n- In 1998, the film Angaaray starred Akshay Kumar, Nagarjuna, Pooja Bhatt, and Sonali Bendre in lead roles.\n- In 1998, the film Angaaray had music composed by Anu Malik and Aadesh Shrivastava.\n- In the 1990s, Akshay Kumar’s films Lahu Ke Do Rang, Insaaf, Daava, Tarazu, Angaaray, Barood, and Zulmi performed poorly at the box office and caused a setback in his film career.\n- In 2005, Garam Masala was released as an Indian comedy film directed by Priyadarshan.\n- In 2005, Garam Masala featured Akshay Kumar, John Abraham, Rimi Sen, Neha Dhupia, Paresh Rawal, and Rajpal Yadav.\n- Aadesh Shrivastava died of cancer at Kokilaben Hospital one day after turning 51.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
